# Keep the build context small AND keep secrets/local state out of the image.
#
# .env is the important line here: the Dockerfile does `COPY . .` into the
# builder stage, so without this entry the real Twilio/OpenAI credentials
# would be baked into an image layer — readable by anyone who can pull the
# image, and not removable by a later RUN rm. Production config is injected
# as Railway environment variables instead; nothing secret belongs in the
# build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local SQLite databases. ./amaaii.db may back a live local demo server, and
# in production the database lives on a mounted volume at /data — a copy
# baked into the image would be shadowed at best, and stale user data
# shipped into a container at worst.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Regenerated inside the builder; copying host artifacts risks mixing a
# host-built native binding (wrong ABI/platform) into the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
apps/web/out
apps/web/.next

# Not needed to build or run the server.
.git
.gitignore
.github
tests
scripts/smoke
coverage
*.log
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Docs and planning material — excluded so an edit to a markdown file
# doesn't invalidate the Docker layer cache and force a full rebuild.
*.md
!README.md
graphify-out
